    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "By pouring the same amount of water into two bottles of the same diameter but different height, one of them is filled to half its height and the other is filled to a third of its height. How much taller is one bottle relative to the other?",
    "image": null,
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "10%"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "25%"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "50%"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "75%"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "100%"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "C",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Equal water levels",
        "body": "The bottles have the same diameter and contain the same amount of water, so the water stands at the same height $w$ in both. The first bottle has height $2w$, the second $3w$. The second is taller by $w$, which is $\\frac{w}{2w} = 50\\%$ of the height of the first.\n\n**Answer: (C) 50%**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Numbers",
        "body": "Let the water be 10 cm high in both bottles. Then the bottles are 20 cm and 30 cm high, and 30 cm is 10 cm, i.e. $50\\%$, more than 20 cm.\n\n**Answer: (C) 50%**"
      }
    ],
    "topics": [
